    "q": "<p>Korea's PPF is x/30 + y/10 = 1 and Vietnam's PPF is x/60 + y/12 = 1 (x = rice, y = phones). Find each country's maximum output and make the opportunity-cost table for both countries. Which country's PPF is flatter?</p>",
    "a": "<p>x/a + y/b = 1: a = max rice, b = max phones. Korea: 30 rice or 10 phones. Vietnam: 60 rice or 12 phones.</p><p>Cost of 1 unit = max of the other good ÷ max of this good.</p><table><tr><th></th><th>Korea</th><th>Vietnam</th></tr><tr><td>One rice</td><td>10/30 = 1/3 phone</td><td>12/60 = 1/5 phone</td></tr><tr><td>One phone</td><td>30/10 = 3 rice</td><td>60/12 = 5 rice</td></tr></table><p>For each country the two numbers are upside-down of each other (3 and 1/3; 5 and 1/5). With rice on the x axis, Vietnam's line is <b>flatter</b> (it gives up only 1/5 phone per rice): rice is cheap there.</p>"
